accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  updated  type  surgical pathology  pathology report   removed_accession_id   massachusetts general hospital  boston  ma  removed_case_id  tel  617  removed_date    surgical pathology report      accession     removed_accession_id    removed_patient_name  m   dob  removed_date  age  62   sex  f  mrn   removed_case_id   location  pac  institution  mgh  date of operation  removed_date  date of accession  removed_date  reported  removed_date 13 01  results to   michelle connolly specht md      final pathologic diagnosis   a  right breast wire localized excision   in situ neoplasia with mixed lobular and ductal features  present in 16 of 21  blocks  and present at or within 0 1cm from the margin in multiple foci   see  note    atypical ductal hyperplasia   focal flat epithelial atypia associated with mucin   fibrocystic changes   small hyalinized fibroadenoma   healing biopsy site   scattered small calcifications in benign lobules and in the in situ neoplasia     note  the prior core biopsy  see  removed_accession_id   shows high grade  grade 2 3   carcinoma in situ which is clearly ductal type  i e   dcis  there is no  residual similar lesion in any of the current specimens  there are however  extensive foci of in situ neoplasia which morphologically favor lobular  neoplasia based on the dyshesive appearance of the cells and the architectural  growth pattern  the nuclear atypia ranges from grade 1 to 2  focally the  neoplastic cells show florid duct distension  most of the foci are positive for  e cadherin  although some are negative  the e cadherin positive versus negative  foci cannot be distinguished morphologically  representative foci show mostly  positive her2 staining as well  which is unusual for lobular neoplasia  the  quality of the staining is somewhat clumped on the membrane  and not the same as  the sharp linear membrane staining seen in the dcis in the prior core biopsy   the her2 results in this material are used only to suggest it is different from  both classic lobular neoplasia and from the patient s dcis in the prior biopsy   it is not to be interpreted as her2 status  although the lesion in the current  material may represent the rare e cadherin positive lobular neoplasia  it is  unknown whether that lesion is biologically more akin to lobular or ductal  neoplasia  the degree of proliferation in the foci throughout parts a through e  ranges from hyperplasia to carcinoma  however  for practical purposes  the  lesion throughout may be best considered a non classic form of lobular carcinoma  in situ for which some consideration of treatment as for dcis applies  hormone  receptor studies will be performed on representative foci  block  removed_accession_id   and the  results reported in an addendum  an immunostain for keratin5 6 was reviewed as  part of the evaluation     b  right breast excision  medial final margin   in situ neoplasia with mixed lobular and ductal features  present in 4 of 4  blocks  and 0 05cm from the margin   atypical ductal hyperplasia   healing biopsy site     note  the neoplastic cells are positive for e cadherin in some foci  including  close to the margin  and negative in others  the cells show mixed but mostly  positive staining for her2  the pattern of mostly negative staining for  keratin5 6 supports atypical ductal hyperplasia     c  right breast excision  superior final margin   in situ neoplasia with mixed lobular and ductal features  present in 2 of 4  blocks  and   0 05cm from the margin     note  the neoplastic cells are positive for e cadherin and show mixed positive  and negative staining for her2     d  right breast excision  anterior final margin   in situ neoplasia with mixed lobular and ductal features  present in 3 of 4  blocks  and   0 05cm from the margin     note  the neoplastic cells are positive for e cadherin in some foci  including  by the margin  and negative in other foci  the cells show a mixed positive and  negative pattern of her2 staining     e  right breast excision  inferior final margin   in situ neoplasia with mixed lobular and ductal features  present in 3 of 4  blocks  and focally present at the margin   small hyalinized fibroadenoma   healing biopsy site     note  the neoplastic cells are positive for e cadherin in most foci  including  at the margin  and negative in a few foci  but both types of foci show a similar  pattern of positive her2 staining        electronically signed out by kristina m braaten md           by his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the final diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       procedures addenda    hormone receptor quantitation  ordered date  removed_date    a  right breast wire localized excision   block tested   removed_accession_id   the in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   some in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein     note   estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  the percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     the tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     the tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained                electronically signed out by  atul k bhan mbbs  md on removed_date 16 15       clinical history  dcis     specimens submitted   a  breast excision  right  b  breast excision  right medial final margin  c  breast excision  right superior final margin  d  breast excision  right anterior final margin  e  breast excision  right inferior final margin    gross description  a  received fresh   labeled remove_patient_name  connor    removed_case_id     right breast needle  localized lumpectomy   is a removed_date x removed_date x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with  a localization wire in place  which