accession number   removed_accession_id   removed_case_id  report status  signed  type  surgical pathology  procedure date  removed_date  diagnosis   left breast  needle biopsy at 12 o clock   carcinoma in situ  indeterminate whether lobular or ductal   foreign body reaction with cholesterol clefts   note  e cadherin stain is mixed positive and negative in the carcinoma in  situ   the case was referred to dr  frederick koerner  massachusetts general  hospital  who made the following comments    the underlying tissue in this core biopsy specimen contains a collection  of debris and histiocytes  which one might see as a consequence of rupture  of a duct  a uniform population of atypical epithelial cells fills and  distends the acini in an adjacent lobules  the cells appear enlarged and  they contain slightly enlarged nuclei  homogeneous chromatin   inconspicuous nucleoli  and modest amounts of eosinophilic cytoplasm  the  cells do not appear polarized nor do they form cribriform spaces  instead   they grow as a sheet of polygonal cells  although these findings  establish the diagnosis of carcinoma in situ  they do not allow me to  identify the nature of the malignant cells  the stain for e cadherin  presents a complicated picture  the residual luminal cells of the acini  show strong  linear staining for the protein  and the residual  myoepithelial cells stain with a fainter  granular  and interrupted  pattern  slight proliferation and off center planes of section make the  myoepithelial cells seem especially numerous  among these preexisting  benign cells sit the carcinoma cells  which fail to stain for e cadherin   i would therefore conclude that the carcinoma in situ most likely  represents lobular carcinoma in situ  because of the complexity of the  immunohistochemical staining pattern and the small size of the focus  it  strikes me as prudent to postpone classification of the carcinoma in situ  until one can study an excision specimen through    immunohistochemical staining on the formalin fixed  paraffin embedded  block reveals these results for the ductal carcinoma in situ   estrogen receptor  positive   10  of nuclei stained   final diagnosis by  richard j  sampson  m d   clinical diagnosis   history   status post left breast  previous benign biopsy  left  cancer   complicated cyst  fibroadenoma  tissue designation   breast  needle biopsy   left  12 o clock  gross description   the specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  guided breast  biopsies  left breast  and consists of a removed_date x removed_date x 0 2cm  aggregate of soft   tan pink  glistening needle biopsies measuring 0 2cm  in diameter each  1  agg  all   dictated by  lv____ signature on file ____dennis j  feen  m d  removed_date  final   ____ signature on file ____richard sampson  m d  removed_date  final    report_end  , benign.
