accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final  type  surgical pathology  specimen type  breast  excisional tissue  procedure date  removed_date  ordering provider  esther rhei m d   case  bs 08  removed_accession_id    removed_patient_name   resident  shakti ramkissoon  m d   ph d   pathologist  susan lester  m d   ph d   pathologic diagnosis   left breast  wire localized excision for a removed_date cm mass and a clip marking a  prior core needle biopsy site   invasive ductal carcinoma  well differentiated  modified bloom richardson  grade i iii   2 1cm  with secretory features  see note   immunoperoxidase  studies for p63 and smooth muscle myosin heavy chain with cytokeratin  removed_accession_id   removed_accession_id   confirm the absence of myoepithelial cells in areas of invasive carcinoma   blocks  removed_accession_id  and  removed_accession_id    focal  removed_accession_id  positivity is present  the nests of tumor  cells show collagen iv deposition   no lymphovascular invasion is seen   no carcinoma in situ is seen  eic negative    the core needle biopsy site is present within the carcinoma   invasive carcinoma is present at the deep medial margin with cautery  present on the carcinoma  invasive carcinoma is   0 1cm from the lateral  margin over a broad front and 0 2cm from the superior margin  invasive  carcinoma is not seen close to the anterior and inferior margins   immunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for  invasive carcinoma  blocks  removed_accession_id  and  removed_accession_id     estrogen receptor negative    1   very weak   progesterone receptor negative    1   very weak    removed_accession_id  neu negative  0   note  the carcinoma has a very unusual appearance  the cells have clear  to apocrine granular appearing cytoplasm and form rounded tubules  the  tubules are arranged in nests  mimicking lobule formation  little stromal  reaction is present  in the excisional specimen  the carcinoma invades around  residual normal ducts and lobules  many of the tubules are filled with a  thick secretory material that shows frequent calcification   the prior core needle biopsy showed similar features  but there was less  lesional tissue for evaluation  reviewed as  removed_accession_id    the original er and  pr studies on the core needle biopsy were reported as negative  the repeat  studies performed at bwh on the core needle biopsy showed weak positivity   the studies on the excisional specimen show only very focal weak er and pr  positivity  but there is very strong positivity for er and pr in the  surrounding normal breast tissue  this is considered a negative result for  er and pr   in addition to the tubular areas  there are some areas of solid nests of  cells infiltrative in stroma  there is focal moderate to marked nuclear  atypia   the carcinoma has some features similar to microglandular adenosis   however  due to the predominant pattern of clustered tubules  solid nests of  tumor  and nuclear pleomorphism  this lesion is best classified as an  invasive carcinoma   this carcinoma would be classified as ajcc  6th edition   removed_accession_id  nx   clinical data   history  46 year old peri menopausal woman  s p l breast core bx on removed_date  revealing atypical glandular proliferation and r breast mammo removed_date revealing  grouped punctate and amorphous calcifications in r uoq  not amenable to core  bx  previous surgery  removed_date    reviewed as  removed_accession_id     operation  r breast wl bx and exc l breast mass with wire localization   operative findings  not provided   clinical diagnosis  see above   tissue submitted   a 1  left breast tissue  short superior  long lateral  whip stitch chest wall  margin   radiology   specimen  1 left breast  mass clip present   wire hook intact  called to dr   rhei by dr  ritner removed_date at 4 50 am   gross description   the specimen is received fresh  in two parts  each  labeled remove_patient_name  patient 