accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final  type  surgical pathology  pathology report  removed_accession_id  breast   excisional tissue w margins  accessioned on  removed_date  richardson  andrea  l   m d  ph d   diagnosis  by richardson andrea l  m d  ph d   right breast wire localized excision for calcifications and a mass   invasive carcinoma  see note   the carcinoma measures 0 7cm   by modified bloom richardson criteria  the carcinoma is grade ii of iii   no lymphovascular invasion seen   ductal carcinoma in situ comedo and solid type  high nuclear grade  with  necrosis and calcifications   dcis is adjacent to the invasive carcinoma and is also away from the  invasive carcinoma in 8 of 18 blocks   invasive carcinoma is greater than 0 3cm from margins   dcis is in lobules at the lateral margin  block 11  and within 0 1cm  of anterior  block 11   other margins are greater than 0 3cm   immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor  progesterone  receptor  and  removed_accession_id  neu will be performed and reported in an addendum   note  the invasive carcinoma is characterized around the periphery by  solid nests or balls of cells with a basaloid appearance  some peripheral  palisading  with clearing of the cytoplasm and intracytoplasmic vacuoles   and moderate nuclear atypia  in the central area  the tumor  shows more infiltrative trabecula within a desmoplastic stroma  the  irregular trabecular areas have a biphasic appearance with similar  malignant baseloid cells surrounding small ductules of eosinophilic cells   some of the tumor nests show round pseudocystic spaces filled with a  myxoid substance  immunohistochemical stains for smooth muscle actin  demonstrate the absence of actin positive myoepithelial cells around the  infiltrative or round cell nests supporting the invasive nature of the  lesion  the tumor cells themselves are negative for sma   immunohistochemistry for p63  a presumed myoepithelial or basal cell  marker  show that the solid balls of tumor cells are mostly to all  positive for p63  within the biphasic trabecular areas  many of the  baseloid appearing cells are positive for p63 and the central eosinophilic  ductules are negative  this finding may suggest a myoepithelial  differentiation  the adjacent high grade dcis has a slighly different  cytologic appearance and a higher nuclear grade   the histologic features are very unusual and the lesion is difficult to  classify with certainty  the features are felt to be most consistent with  a solid varient of adenoid cystic carcinoma with baseloid features  this  entity in the breast has been recently reported and described by shin and  rosen  am  j  surgical pathology  26 4   removed_date   removed_case_id   the prognosis of  this lesion is uncertain but may not be the better prognosis associated  with typical adenoid cystic carcinomas   this case was also reviewed by drs  susan lester  stuart schnitt and james  connolly   surgical addendum  by lester susan m d  ph d   immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for invasive carcinoma  block 2    estrogen receptor negative  progesterone receptor negative   removed_accession_id  neu  c erb  removed_accession_id   negative  0   note  normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen  and progesterone receptors   interpretation   hormone receptor analysis  the percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the  invasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low  0  to  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  nuclei immunoreactive  the lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet  been determined    removed_accession_id  neu analysis   negative  0   no immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   negative  1    faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but  only a portion of the membrane is positive   positive  2    weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells   positive  3    moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity  in  10  of tumor cells   cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational  use only   clinical data   history  a 51 year old female with calcifications and density in right medial  breast  patient has not had core biopsy   operation  right mammographically directed biopsy  clinical diagnosis  abnormal mammogram right breast tissue  short   superior  long   lateral   radiology  calcifications and density in specimen  e  sedgwick md  gross description  by abbott derek w m d  ph d   the specimen is received fresh   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and   1  right breast tissue  and consists of a fragment of fibrofatty breast  tissue  4 3 x removed_date x 2 1cm    the specimen is marked by a short stitch marking  the superior aspect of the specimen and a long stitch marking the lateral  aspect of the specimen  the specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the  evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior   blue  superior   red   inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange  the specimen is serially  sectioned to reveal a small cystic structure  0 6 x removed_date x 0 2cm   lying grossly  greater than 0 5cm from the superior  inferior  medial and deep margins  the  remainder of the breast contains fatty tissue  the specimen is entirely  submitted for histologic analysis   micro removed_date  small cystic area of breast  1 frag each  rss  micro removed_date  remainder of specimen  1 frag each  ess  dwa  reports to  carter  katharine m d   specimen type  breast   excisional tissue w margins   report_end  , benign.
