accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final  type  surgical pathology  pathology report  removed_accession_id   accessioned on  removed_date  lester  susan  m d  ph d   diagnosis  by lester susan m d  ph d   consult slides from harvard community health plan  boston  ma   right breast biopsy  s 95  removed_case_id   10 17 95    invasive ductal carcinoma  well differentiated  modified bloom   richardson grade i of iii  present as multiple foci  the largest measuring  0 3cm in greatest dimension  blocks a  b  and c   see note   no lymphatic  vascular invasion seen  no in situ carcinoma is present within the area of  the invasive tumor   ductal carcinoma in situ  papillary type  intermediate nuclear grade   present as a single 0 7cm friable mass surrounded by desmoplastic stromal  response  chronic inflammation and fat necrosis   epithelial hyperplasia  mild  with tall cell change   fibrocystic changes including large cysts and adenosis   note  this biopsy is difficult to interpret due to the nature of the lesion  and the degree of fragmentation  the main lesion consists of fragments of  papillary architecture without an evident myoepithelial cell layer  these  fragments appear to occupy a space surrounded by a reactive stromal response  and fat necrosis  a definite capsule is not seen and definite invasion of  this lesion into stroma is not seen  due to the papillary appearance of the  cells in islands devoid of stroma  this area is interpreted as a focus of  papillary carcinoma in situ  carcinoma in situ is not seen outside of this  area   adjacent to this area are smaller foci of invasive carcinoma  it is  difficult to give an exact size because these foci are present in multiple  slides  and may represent either a single focus or multiple foci   however   the largest contiguous focus is 0 3cm in size   due to the fragmented nature of the specimen  margins cannot be evaluated   clinical data   history  well circumscribed palpable mass also seen on m